h hydantoin diversion\",\n      \"description\": \"The most speculative sequence: hypothesized precyclization dehydration and formamidine capture are followed by an unvalidated histidine-specific hydantoin pathway. Included as an explicitly testable alternative, not as experimental evidence.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_007\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_008\", \"rxn_009\", \"rxn_010\", \"rxn_013\", \"rxn_014\", \"rxn_015\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_010\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_013\", \"mol_016\", \"mol_017\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydrogen-containing reduced-gas electrical-discharge route\",\n      \"description\": \"Experimentally reported histidine endpoint from CH4/NH3/H2/H2O discharge chemistry. Molecular intermediates remain unresolved, so the path is represented by one empirical multistep reaction node.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_016\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P10\",\n      \"name\": \"Nitrogen-containing reduced-gas electrical-discharge route\",\n      \"description\": \"Experimentally reported histidine assignment from CH4/NH3/N2/H2O discharge chemistry without supplied H2. This differs from P9 in feedstock regime, not in a demonstrated target-specific mechanism; no direct incorporation of N2 into histidine is presumed.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_017\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hub_molecules\": [\n    \"mol_006\",\n    \"mol_007\",\n    \"mol_008\",\n    \"mol_009\",\n    \"mol_013\",\n    \"mol_018\"\n  ],\n  \"convergence_points\": [\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_006\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_001\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_006\", \"rxn_007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_007\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_002\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_008\"]\n   