carbon and nitrogen chemistry followed by aqueous accumulation and amino-acid analysis. Hydrogen appears on both sides because it is a feed gas and a formal redox-balancing pool in this selected-product projection.", "reasoning": "Jiang et al. (2014) reported 17 natural amino acids after seven days, describing all non-sulfur protein amino acids except glutamate, which includes histidine. Analysis used derivatization and LC-MS/MS against amino-acid standards, but the supplied record gives no absolute histidine yield or target-specific mechanism. Consequently, this source term is not routed through erythrose or imidazole-4-acetaldehyde. Continuous energy input, replenished reduced gases, and laboratory gas retention are important boundary conditions, not demonstrated natural steady states. No measured net H2 yield is implied."}], "pathways": [{"pathway_id": "P1", "name": "Precursor-fed Shen synthesis", "description": "Begin with supplied D-erythrose and formamidine, generate imidazole-4-acetaldehyde, and complete the Strecker sequence. The experimental overall precursor-to-histidine connection is supported; separately represented aminonitrile capture and proposed environmental hydrolysis conditions are not independently validated. External precursor availability remains conditional.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_009"]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "name": "Glycolaldehyde-fed extension of the Shen pathway", "description": "Generate an erythrose-containing mixture by glycolaldehyde self-aldol chemistry, then enter the shared Shen sequence. Productive erythrose concentration, selection, preservation, and transfer have not been demonstrated. This is a conditional upstream extension, not an independently validated complete synthesis.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_003", "mol_008", "mol_009"]}, {"pathway_id": "P3", "name": "Formaldehyde-fed formose extension of the Shen pathway", "description": "Use formaldehyde and glycolaldehyde in an alkaline formose branch, then transfer an erythrose fraction into the shared imidazole and Strecker chemistry. The end-to-end sequence is unvalidated; incompatible reaction stages and sugar instability are explicit bottlenecks.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_003", "mol_008", "mol_009"]}, {"pathway_id": "P4", "name": "Buffered mineral-independent discharge protocol", "description": "Criado-Reyes et al. (2021), buffered Teflon-only configuration. This is a reported empirical endpoint pathway with unresolved intermediates and qualified GC-MS identification.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_006"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "name": "Buffered borosilicate-contact discharge protocol", "description": "Criado-Reyes et al. (2021), buffered borosilicate-reactor configuration. Distinct experimental surface conditions do not establish a distinct histidine mechanism.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_007"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "name": "Buffered mixed-wall discharge protocol", "description": "Criado-Reyes et al. (2021), buffered Teflon reactor containing borosilicate pieces. An operational surface-contact variant of the same unresolved discharge family.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_008"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "name": "Initially alkaline mineral-independent discharge protocol", "description": "Criado-Reyes et al. (2021), unbuffered Teflon-only configuration. Initial alkalinity distinguishes the protocol, but a separate molecular pathway has not been established.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_009"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P8", "name": "Initially alkaline borosilicate-contact discharge protocol", "description": "Criado-Reyes et al. (2021), unbuffered borosilicate-reactor configuration. Histidine is a reported analytical endpoint; glass-specific target catalysis is not demonstrated.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P9", "name": "Initially alkaline mixed-wall discharge protocol", "description": "Criado-Reyes et al. (2021), unbuffered Teflon reactor with borosilicate pieces. Shares mechanistic and analytical uncertainties with P4-P8 and is not independent confirmation of another synthesis family.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_011"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P10", "name": "Hydrogen-containing seven-day discharge protocol", "description": "Jiang et al. (2014), methane-ammonia-hydrogen-water discharge with replenished gases. Histidine is included in the reported amino-acid inventory, but no target-specific intermediate sequence or absolute histidine yield is established in the supplied record.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": []}], "hub_molecules": ["mol_002", "mol_003", "mol_005", "mol_007", "mol_010", "mol_011", "mol_012", "mol_013"], "convergence_points": [{"molecule_id": "mol_003", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_003"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_005", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_005"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_004", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010", "rxn_011", "rxn_012"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_007", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_003", "rxn_004"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010", "rxn_011", "rxn_012"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_010", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010", "rxn_011", "rxn_012"], "outgoing_reactions": []}, {"molecule_id": "mol_012", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010", "rxn_011", "rxn_012"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_012"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_013", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010", "rxn_011"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010", "